@* WASP Bzzz — the public front door, rendered full-width inside the marketing
   shell (sg-nav + sg-footer) defined in Program.WrapWithSidebar for path "/".
   One integrated Blazor app: this page and /chat share the same canister.
   Editorial-precision design + on-chain "proof" devices. Every feature shown is
   genuinely shipped (Chat/Server/Mod/Dm/Role/Membership services). All product
   visuals are CSS/SVG mockups — no <img>, no fabricated metrics/logos. The live
   canister id comes from AdminService.CanisterIdText(), never hardcoded. *@

<PageTitle>WASP Bzzz — chat that lives on-chain</PageTitle>

@* ── Hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-hero" id="top">
    <div class="sg-hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="sg-hero-grid">
        <div class="sg-hero-copy">
            <span class="sg-eyebrow"><span class="sg-dot"></span>Runs entirely on the Internet Computer</span>
            <h1 class="sg-h1">Chat with no backend to trust.<br />One canister. Every message <span class="sg-grad">signed</span>.</h1>
            <p class="sg-lead">WASP&nbsp;Bzzz is a Discord-style community platform that runs entirely inside one Internet Computer canister. No servers, no database, no passwords — every action is a signed transaction you can verify.</p>
            <div class="sg-cta-row">
                <button type="button" class="sg-btn sg-btn-primary ii-signin" data-ii-signin><span class="ii-mark">∞</span> Sign in with Internet Identity</button>
                <a class="sg-btn sg-btn-ghost" href="/chat">Open the app →</a>
            </div>
            <p class="sg-hero-note">free · no email · no password · no wallet</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-hero-mock">
            <div class="sg-dotgrid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            @MockWindow(false)
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Proof strip (honest facts, no invented metrics) ────── *@
<section class="sg-section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="sg-proof-cells">
        <div class="sg-fact"><span class="sg-fact-l">@Seal(13) Auth</span><div class="sg-fact-v">Internet Identity — no password</div></div>
        <div class="sg-fact"><span class="sg-fact-l">@Seal(13) Writes</span><div class="sg-fact-v">Signed update calls</div></div>
        <div class="sg-fact"><span class="sg-fact-l">@Seal(13) Caller</span><div class="sg-fact-v">Verified <code>msg_caller</code></div></div>
        <div class="sg-fact"><span class="sg-fact-l">@Seal(13) Reads</span><div class="sg-fact-v">Certified responses</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-chip-wrap">
        <span class="sg-chip" title="The live canister this site is served from">@Seal(14) <b>canister</b> @canisterId</span>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Big visual: the product, shown big ─────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-section" id="features">
    <div class="sg-shead sg-reveal">
        <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">The product</span>
        <h2 class="sg-h2">Servers, channels, threads.</h2>
        <p class="sg-sintro">A real workspace, not a demo. Servers hold channels; channels hold threads; everything is a signed message living inside the canister.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-bigvis sg-reveal">
        @MockWindow(true)
        <div class="sg-callrow">
            <span class="sg-call"><i style="background:var(--sg-accent)"></i><b>Threads</b> keep replies linked</span>
            <span class="sg-call"><i style="background:var(--sg-proof)"></i><b>Reactions</b> on any message</span>
            <span class="sg-call"><i style="background:var(--sg-warn)"></i><b>Role badges</b> enforced on-chain</span>
            <span class="sg-call"><i style="background:var(--sg-text-3)"></i><b>Pinned</b> &amp; lockable channels</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Deep-dive A: roles & moderation ────────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-section sg-band" id="roles">
    <div class="sg-deep">
        <div class="sg-deep-copy sg-reveal">
            <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">Roles &amp; moderation</span>
            <h2 class="sg-h2">Enforced on-chain, not in the UI.</h2>
            <p class="sg-sintro">Owners, admins and moderators get real powers — and the canister checks who you are before every privileged action. There is no API to go around.</p>
            <ul class="sg-list">
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Four tiers.</b> Owner, admin, moderator, member — granted per server.</span></li>
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Pin, lock, time-out.</b> Moderation actions are signed update calls, authorised by your principal.</span></li>
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Tamper-proof.</b> A locked channel rejects posts at the canister, not just the button.</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-deep-visual sg-reveal">
            <div class="sg-panel">
                <div class="sg-members">
                    <div class="sg-member"><span class="sg-pres"></span><span class="sg-mname2">Ada</span><span class="role owner">Owner</span></div>
                    <div class="sg-member"><span class="sg-pres"></span><span class="sg-mname2">Mira</span><span class="role admin">Admin</span></div>
                    <div class="sg-member"><span class="sg-pres idle"></span><span class="sg-mname2">Kai</span><span class="role mod">Mod</span></div>
                    <div class="sg-member"><span class="sg-pres off"></span><span class="sg-mname2">Jun</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="sg-modmenu">
                    <div class="mi">@Svg("<path d='M12 17v5'/><path d='M9 3h6l-1 6 3 3H7l3-3-1-6z'/>", 17) Pin message</div>
                    <div class="mi warn">@Svg("<rect x='5' y='11' width='14' height='9' rx='2'/><path d='M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3'/>", 17) Lock channel</div>
                    <div class="mi">@Svg("<circle cx='12' cy='12' r='9'/><path d='M12 7v5l3 2'/>", 17) Time-out user</div>
                </div>
                <div class="sg-lockban">@Svg("<rect x='5' y='11' width='14' height='9' rx='2'/><path d='M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3'/>", 15) #founders is locked — only moderators can post</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Deep-dive B: rich messages ─────────────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-section" id="richmsg">
    <div class="sg-deep reverse">
        <div class="sg-deep-copy sg-reveal">
            <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">Rich messages</span>
            <h2 class="sg-h2">Markdown, code, spoilers, media.</h2>
            <p class="sg-sintro">Say it properly. Format with markdown, drop in fenced code, hide spoilers, react with emoji, and share images and video — all rendered inline, all stored on-chain.</p>
            <ul class="sg-list">
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Markdown &amp; code.</b> Bold, italic, lists and syntax-tinted code blocks.</span></li>
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Spoilers.</b> Blur text until a reader chooses to look.</span></li>
                <li class="sg-li">@Seal() <span><b>Media.</b> Image uploads and embedded video, no external host.</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-deep-visual sg-reveal">
            <div class="sg-panel sg-rich">
                <p class="sg-mtext">Release notes for <b>v3</b> — <i>everything</i> ships today:</p>
                <div class="sg-code"><span class="c">// every write is authorised on-chain</span><br /><span class="k">if</span> (msg.author == <span class="s">caller</span>) commit(msg);</div>
                <p class="sg-mtext">Ending is: <span class="sg-spoiler">it was on-chain all along</span> — hover to reveal.</p>
                <div class="sg-imgtile">image upload · stored in the canister</div>
                <div class="sg-video"><span class="sg-play">@Svg("<path d='M8 5l11 7-11 7z' fill='currentColor' stroke='none'/>", 18)</span></div>
                <div class="sg-react-row"><span class="sg-react on">✅ 4</span><span class="sg-react">🔥 7</span><span class="sg-react">🎉 2</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Deep-dive C: private means private ─────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-section sg-band" id="security">
    <div class="sg-shead sg-reveal">
        <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">Private means private</span>
        <h2 class="sg-h2">A lock that isn't decorative.</h2>
        <p class="sg-sintro">Private servers and DMs are returned <em>only</em> to their members, over signed reads — never rendered to the public, cacheable web. Not privacy by obscurity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-privacy sg-reveal">
        <div class="sg-priv pub">
            <span class="sg-priv-seal">@Svg("<rect x='5' y='11' width='14' height='9' rx='2'/><path d='M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3'/>", 16)</span>
            <div class="sg-priv-tag">@Svg("<path d='M3 3l18 18'/><path d='M10.6 10.6a3 3 0 0 0 4 4'/><path d='M9.9 4.2A9 9 0 0 1 21 12a9 9 0 0 1-2.2 2.9'/><path d='M6.6 6.6A9 9 0 0 0 3 12a9 9 0 0 0 9 6'/>", 14) Public web · SSR</div>
            <div class="sg-priv-rows">
                <div class="sg-priv-line w2"></div><div class="sg-priv-line w1"></div><div class="sg-priv-line w3"></div><div class="sg-priv-line w4"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="sg-priv-foot">Never served to the public web.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-priv mem">
            <span class="sg-priv-seal">@Seal(16)</span>
            <div class="sg-priv-tag">@Seal(14) Members-only · signed read</div>
            <div class="sg-priv-real">
                <div class="sg-msg"><span class="sg-av a">A</span><div><span class="sg-mname">Ada</span><p class="sg-mtext">founders channel — visible to members</p></div></div>
                <div class="sg-msg"><span class="sg-av c">M</span><div><span class="sg-mname">Mira</span><p class="sg-mtext">returned only over a signed read</p></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="sg-priv-foot">Returned to verified members only.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ── Why on-chain: the spec table ───────────────────────── *@
<section class="sg-section" id="chain">
    <div class="sg-shead sg-reveal">
        <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">Why on-chain</span>
        <h2 class="sg-h2">Trust math, not a company.</h2>
        <p class="sg-sintro">The same chat features you expect — but the place they run changes what you have to trust.</p>
    </div>
    <table class="sg-table sg-reveal">
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>Typical chat SaaS</th><th class="chain">WASP Bzzz on the IC</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><th>Where it runs</th><td class="saas">A company's cloud servers</td><td class="chain">@Seal(15)One canister on the Internet Computer</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Who can read your data</th><td class="saas">The operator and their database</td><td class="chain">@Seal(15)Only members, over signed reads</td></tr>
            <tr><th>If the company disappears</th><td class="saas">Your community goes with it</td><td class="chain">@Seal(15)It runs on-chain, not on us</td></tr>
            <tr><th>How sign-in works</th><td class="saas">Email + password to leak</td><td class="chain">@Seal(15)Internet Identity — no password exists</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Can responses be tampered with</th><td class="saas">Trust the operator's word</td><td class="chain">@Seal(15)Certified by the Internet Computer</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

@* ── Verify it yourself (replaces testimonials) ─────────── *@
<section class="sg-section sg-band" id="verify">
    <div class="sg-shead center sg-reveal">
        <span class="sg-eyebrow plain">Verify it yourself</span>
        <h2 class="sg-h2">Don't trust us. Read the canister.</h2>
        <p class="sg-sintro" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">The honest proof isn't a logo wall — it's that you can inspect the live state we run on.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sg-term sg-reveal" style="margin:0 auto">
        <div class="sg-term-bar"><span class="sg-tdot r"></span><span class="sg-tdot y"></span><span class="sg-tdot g"></span><span class="sg-term-title">verify — WASP Bzzz</span></div>
        <div class="sg-term-body">
            <div class="sg-term-num">1<br />2<br />3<br />4<br />5<br />6<br />7</div>
            <div class="sg-term-code"><span class="c">$ inspect this canister</span><br />canister&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>@canisterId</b><br />state&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="p">certified by the Internet Computer</span><br />reads&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="p">certified</span> · writes <span class="p">signed update calls</span><br />auth&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Internet Identity · caller = <span class="a">msg_caller</span><br /><a class="sg-term-link" href="/stable">→ view certified stable state</a><br /><span class="sg-caret">▋</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

